
		D U N E     (with apologies to Frank Herbert)

You are in a strange, barren world consisting of nothing but sand dunes that
stretch in all directions as far as the eye can see ...

After a little exploration you discover that this world is rectangular!  It is
bounded on the north, south, east and west by high cliffs formed from a glassy
substance which you cannot climb.

As you wander you discover that:
  a) Periodically a large bag of `spice' appears on the surface of the dunes,
  b) There is a hole which probably leads back where you came from.
  c) An immense WORM prowls around ready to eat anyone who desecrates the
     sacred spice bags.
You also observe that:
  d) The worm shows great deference to the bags of spice and the hole and will
     not pass over, (or under), them.

The symbols used to represent the various objects on Dune are:
    U       You
    $       A bag of spice
    O       The hole leading home [?]
    oooo@   The Worm

Your motion is controlled by six keys on the terminal:
  4  --  move left, west
  6  --  move right, east
  8  --  move up, north
  2  --  move down, south
  h  --  move horizontally until you are directly N or S of the spice
  v  --  move vertically until you are directly E or W of the spice
Several other keys have special meaning:
  $  --  drop a bag of spice where you are
  ^  --  re-draw the screen
  n  --  stop displaying motion on the screen
  d  --  resume displaying motion on the screen
  H  --  equivalent to `nhd'
  V  --  equivalent to `nvd'
Collect as much spice as you dare ...

